--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
kev  (vendored subset)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev
Commit:  90990a5fac2995b9faa3190f7d437e84f2067768  (2026-09-21)
License: Apache License 2.0
Author:  Jared Palmer

Vendored verbatim, with NO local modifications, into
src/decis/engines/_kev_vendor/:

  kev/model.py       -> encode(), branch_mask_batch(), PointerHead, DecisionModel
  kev/checkpoint.py  -> Checkpoint, Meta, LoadOptions
  LICENSE            -> the Apache-2.0 text, as required by section 4(a)/(d)

The full licence text is at src/decis/engines/_kev_vendor/LICENSE. The sha256 of
each vendored file is recorded in src/decis/engines/_kev_vendor/VENDOR.md and is
checked by tests/test_kev_vendor.py, so "were these files modified?" is answerable
without diffing against upstream.

kev/api.py is deliberately NOT vendored: Decis implements the wire contract in
src/decis/schema.py + src/decis/answers.py so that every engine shares one answer
and one confidence definition. kev/serve.py (its HTTP layer) and its training,
evaluation and dataset modules are not used either. See VENDOR.md for the rationale
and for the two os.environ reads that exist in the vendored copy.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
jeff  (vendored subset)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/firelex/jeff
Tag:     v1.1 = f0397f3785d93f73a01411d785d2ed026f53181d  (2026-09-29)
License: MIT License
Authors: Mathias Strasser (Jeff)
         Denis Yarats (AutoJev, on which Jeff's training code is based)

Vendored into src/decis/engines/_jeff_vendor/:

  model.py    -> Content, describe(), options(), decision_messages(),
                 DecisionModel (the Qwen3.5 path)
  decoder.py  -> GenericDecoderDecisionModel (any causal decoder; the Gemma path)
  types.py    -> the decision record TypedDicts
  LICENSE     -> the MIT text, with both copyright notices, as the licence requires

Unlike the kev copy, these are NOT byte-identical to upstream: jeff imports itself
absolutely (`from jeff.types import ...`) and the files have to work as a subpackage
of `decis`. The only difference is that mechanical import rewrite -- `from jeff.X
import` to `from .X import` -- and tests/test_jeff_vendor.py asserts it in both
directions, recomputing the sha256 of every file (the vendored hash *and* the
upstream one are recorded in VENDOR.md).

Deliberately NOT vendored: jeff/server.py (Decis owns the wire contract in
src/decis/schema.py + src/decis/answers.py, so vendoring it would put a second
implementation of the answer format and the confidence formulas in the tree; it
also hardcodes host="127.0.0.1", which breaks container use), and jeff's training,
evaluation, dataset and panel modules. jeff/mlx_backend.py is an Apple-silicon
backend Decis does not use -- every engine serves through torch so that one
DECIS_DEVICE story covers all of them. See VENDOR.md for the full list.

Provenance note: both Jeff checkpoints record the commit
a095c98f3fd2782bba033b378f7375ecc33c35fa in their decision_config.json, which is not
reachable in the public history of the repository. The closest reproducible
revision is the tag above, and only types.py matches both. VENDOR.md records the
discrepancy rather than papering over it.

