--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
djev-run  (the playground's three games: adapted HTML)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/taeold/djev-run
Author:  Daniel Lee (taeold)

playground/web/snake.html, playground/web/dino.html and playground/web/tetris.html
are adapted from that project's pages of the same names. What Decis changed is
listed in each file's header comment and in README.md ("Relationship to other
projects"); in substance: the endpoint is the playground's own origin (so the API
key stays server-side and the browser never holds it), a head-to-head latency
comparison against another deployment was removed rather than re-published with
stale numbers, the Tetris placement question was cut from sixteen verbose options
to five terse ones so that it fits the default engine's per-question token
budget, and the interface was restyled onto a stylesheet shared by all four pages
and translated into Simplified Chinese. The text sent to the model is unchanged:
`state`, `instructions` and `criteria` are still the upstream English strings,
which is also what the token budget above was measured against.

The upstream repository declares no license (it has no LICENSE file), so this
adaptation is recorded as a fact a distributor can act on rather than as a claim
of a grant. The pages themselves derive from projects that repository credits, and
those are recorded here for the same reason:

  Snake  <- https://github.com/mizorewww/laya-coreml
  Dino   <- https://github.com/virajbhartiya/laya-vs-jev   (laya_mlx/trex physics)
  Tetris <- https://github.com/trungdq88/jev-tetris

playground/server.py, playground/index.html and playground/Dockerfile are Decis's
own and carry the Apache-2.0 license at the top of this file.

